      "content": "This is looking really good, the analysis of the color story is spot on.\n\nI'm looking at the draft now and seeing that the discovery score is sitting a bit lower than we usually need for the front page. I know I said not to spam it, but if we can get the brand density up just a little more without it feeling totally fake, that would be ideal. \n\nCould you add one more section? I want to talk about the \"return to heritage\" trend—how older, more classic silhouettes are being reinterpreted. Try to weave in Hermès and any other names from that list that feel relevant to that \"heritage\" vibe. Just be careful—I'll have to defend this to the editor if it looks like we're just dumping names to juice the metric, so keep it sounding professional and analytical.",
